# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Exterior dimensions (2461) on a storey without outer walls: a structural
# plan of a steel hall has only grids, columns and beams. Grids 1 to 4 stand
# at x = 0, 6, 12 and 18 (grid 3 drawn from top to bottom), A and B lie at
# y = 0 and 12. Each family of parallel grids gets a chain of its bays and
# one of its whole, at the low ends of the grids: below 1 to 4 (6000 three
# times, then 18000) and left of A and B (12000 only, a single bay has no
# whole). The extension lines start beyond the grid heads (3 mm on paper,
# 0.3 m at 1:100, off the grids' ends). Undo takes them away, and a storey
# without parallel grids says so.
import ui/editor/bim_editor.dl

function the grid dimensions whole of {a 64 bit floating-point number:amount}:
    execute:
        return (@intrinsic("call", "libc", "round", a 64 bit floating-point number, amount)) as a 64 bit integer

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
type bim editor key 2461 in e
print editor's message as a line
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
begin bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
ignore add bim grid named (the string form of "1") from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y -1.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 13.0) reaching 0.0 to 6.0 to target
ignore add bim grid named (the string form of "2") from (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y -1.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 13.0) reaching 0.0 to 6.0 to target
ignore add bim grid named (the string form of "3") from (a cad vector2 with x 12.0 and y 13.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 12.0 and y -1.0) reaching 0.0 to 6.0 to target
ignore add bim grid named (the string form of "4") from (a cad vector2 with x 18.0 and y -1.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 18.0 and y 13.0) reaching 0.0 to 6.0 to target
ignore add bim grid named (the string form of "A") from (a cad vector2 with x -1.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 19.0 and y 0.0) reaching 0.0 to 6.0 to target
ignore add bim grid named (the string form of "B") from (a cad vector2 with x -1.0 and y 12.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 19.0 and y 12.0) reaching 0.0 to 6.0 to target
commit bim transaction in (the address of (editor's documentValue))
type bim editor key 2461 in e
print editor's message as a line
set modelValue to editor's documentValue's current
set index to the bim join index of modelValue
loop cursor from 0 to the length of (modelValue's dimensions's values):
    set dimensionValue to the item at cursor in (modelValue's dimensions's values)
    set measured to the bim measure of dimensionValue in modelValue using index
    set shape to the bim dimension line of dimensionValue in modelValue using index at drawing scale 100.0
    set described to (the bim length measured's value in units 0) + (the string form of ", ")
    set described to described + ((the string form of (the grid dimensions whole of dimensionValue's paperOffset)) + (the string form of " mm off, feet at mm "))
    set described to described + ((the string form of (the grid dimensions whole of (shape's startFoot's x * 1000.0))) + (the string form of " "))
    set described to described + ((the string form of (the grid dimensions whole of (shape's startFoot's y * 1000.0))) + (the string form of " and "))
    set described to described + ((the string form of (the grid dimensions whole of (shape's finishFoot's x * 1000.0))) + (the string form of " "))
    set described to described + (the string form of (the grid dimensions whole of (shape's finishFoot's y * 1000.0)))
    print described as a line
type bim editor key 90 in e
print ((the string form of "undone: ") + (the string form of (the length of (editor's documentValue's current's dimensions's values)))) as a line
